 2026 | QA Alpha Marketing Spend | Marketing | QAREF-ALPHA-001 | -$250.75 | ✓\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited transaction: description -> \\\"QA Alpha Marketing Spend EDITED\\\", amount 250.75 -> $400.00; row and Total Expenses updated to -$37,009.44. Deleted \\\"QA Missing Category Test\\\" via confirm dialog; row count 20 -> 19 and Total Expenses updated to -$36,885.99.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"QA Test Category\\\" (type Expense, Purple) — Expense Categories count 8->9. Edited to name \\\"QA Renamed Category\\\" with Orange colour (swatch became rgba(249,115,22)). Deleted it via confirmation — category removed and count back to 8.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Assigned category not retained when updating an income transaction; edit dialog fails to prefill category and silently clears it on save\", \"actual\": \"Type/category compatibility itself is correct (Expense lists only expense categories, Income only income categories). However the assigned category is not retained on update for income transactions: \\\"QA Beta Consulting Income\\\" was created with category Consulting (table showed \\\"Consulting\\\"; Categories page counted it under Consulting 4 txns/$11,800), then I edited it changing only the Tax Related switch — afterwards its Category cell is blank. Root cause confirmed: the Edit Transaction dialog does not prefill the category for income transactions — seeded \\\"Consulting Fee - Strategy Session\\\" (table: Consulting) and \\\"Product Sales - Q4 Order\\\" (table: Sales Revenue) both open with the category showing \\\"Select category\\\", while expense transactions (\\\"Electric Bill\\\"/Utilities, \\\"QA Gamma Utility Bill\\\"/Utilities) prefill correctly. Saving any income transaction therefore silently wipes its category.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"QA Alpha\\\" with the Tax Related switch on -> row showed ✓; created \\\"QA Beta\\\" with it off -> blank Tax cell. Via edit, marked QA Beta (blank -> ✓) and unmarked QA Alpha (✓ -> blank). Both directions persisted in the transactions table.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined search=\\\"office\\\" + type=Expense + category=Office Supplies + range 2024-10-01..2024-12-31 returned exactly 2 rows, both satisfying all four criteria. \\\"Clear Filters\\\" reset all controls and restored the full set of 20 transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing required fields block submit silently with no error message shown to user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting with empty Description (amount 99.99, category Software) and separately with empty Amount (description \\\"QA No Amount\\\") both left the dialog open and did not create the transaction (row count stayed 19), but no validation text, toast, or aria-invalid/field-level indicator was rendered anywhere. The user is given no indication of which information is missing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Inverted date range accepted silently with no validation message\", \"actual\": \"Set From=2024-12-31 and To=2024-01-01 (start later than end). The app accepted the range and simply rendered an empty result: \\\"No transactions found / Try adjusting your filters\\\". No rejection, error, or explanation that the date range is invalid was shown.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing category not validated; transaction created with blank category\", \"actual\": \"Submitted Add Transaction with Description \\\"QA Missing Category Test\\\", Amount 123.45 and Category left as \\\"Select category\\\". The dialog closed and the transaction was saved. The new row (Aug 28, 2026) shows an empty Category cell. No error message, toast, or field-level indication of the missing category was shown.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting an in-use category is neither blocked nor offers reassignment; transactions are orphaned with blank category\", \"actual\": \"Deleted the \\\"Marketing\\\" category which showed \\\"2 transactions\\\". The confirm dialog was identical to that for an unused category and even stated \\\"Transactions using this category will not be deleted\\\" — no block and no reassignment option. After deletion, \\\"QA Alpha Marketing Spend EDITED\\\" (-$400.00) and \\\"Google Ads Campaign\\\" (-$850.00) both display an empty Category cell in the transactions table.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding/editing/deleting Aug-2026 transactions in-session, Dashboard immediately showed Monthly Expenses $400, Net Profit/Loss -$400 (deleted $123.45 item correctly excluded) and \\\"QA Alpha Marketing Spend EDITED — Marketing • Aug 28, 2026 — -$400.00\\\" at the top of Recent Transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Before: 2026 Tax Summary showed Deductible Expenses $400.00, Net -$400.00, 1 tax transaction (QA Alpha). After unmarking QA Alpha and marking QA Beta ($1,000 income), the summary updated to Total Taxable Income $1,000.00, Deductible Expenses $0.00, Net Taxable Income $1,000.00, with \\\"All Tax-Related Transactions\\\" listing only QA Beta. Tax status and summary inclusion both tracked the change.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Consulting went from 3 txns/$10,800 to \\\"4 transactions / $11,800\\\" after adding the $1,000 QA Beta income. Marketing shows \\\"2 transactions / $1,250\\\" = original $850 Google Ads + the QA Alpha expense edited from $250.75 to $400, so both creation and modification are reflected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selected year 2024 (selector offers 2022-2026); report rendered fully (Taxable Income $47,592.50, Deductible Expenses $36,485.99, Net $11,106.51, both category breakdowns, 18 tax-related transactions). Clicking \\\"Print Report\\\" invoked window.print() exactly once with no page error thrown and the report still rendered afterwards. No new console errors (only a pre-existing React \\\"unique key prop\\\" dev warning in TaxSummary).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table has Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, Tax columns. Footer shows Total Income +$47,592.50 and Total Expenses -$36,860.19, which match the sum of the displayed rows.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Aug 2026 has exactly two transactions (+$1,000 Consulting income, -$400 Marketing expense). Dashboard showed Monthly Income $1,000-equivalent state and Net matching; Reports for August 2026 showed Total Income $1,000, Total Expenses $400, Net Profit/Loss +$600, Income by Category Consulting $1,000, Expenses by Category Marketing $400 — all accurate. Recent activity listed the correct latest transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart y-axis labels lack precision; non-zero value indistinguishable from zero\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard \\\"Income vs Expenses\\\" chart plots an Aug-2026 expense of $400 (bar rendered at full 216px height), but all 5 y-axis ticks are labelled \\\"$0k\\\". The axis uses whole-thousands ($Xk) formatting, so a $400 value and $0 are labelled identically and cannot be distinguished.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
