    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been executed and recorded.\n\n## Summary\n\n**16 PASS / 6 FAIL**\n\nThe core bookkeeping features work well: transaction CRUD, search, filtering (type/category/date, including combined criteria), category management, dashboards, monthly reports, tax marking, the annual tax summary, and printing all behaved as expected, with summaries and category rollups updating live.\n\n### Failures\n\n**Validation gaps (silent failures)**\n- **CS-13** — Missing description or amount blocks submission, but with *no* message, toast, or field-level indicator. The dialog just sits there.\n- **CS-23** — Worse: a missing category isn't validated at all. The transaction saves with a blank category.\n- **CS-15** — An inverted date range (From 2024-12-31 → To 2024-01-01) is silently accepted and renders \"No transactions found\", implying no data exists rather than flagging the invalid range.\n\n**Data integrity**\n- **CS-24** — Deleting a category in use is neither blocked nor offers reassignment. Deleting \"Marketing\" (2 transactions) orphaned both; they now show blank categories and surface as \"Unknown\" in the tax summary.\n- **FT-9** — The most subtle bug found. Type/category compatibility is correct, but the Edit dialog **fails to prefill the category for income transactions** (expense transactions prefill fine). Saving any income transaction therefore silently wipes its category. I confirmed this on my own transaction (created with Consulting, lost it after only toggling the tax switch) and reproduced it on two untouched seeded income transactions.\n\n**Presentation**\n- **CT-22** — Chart y-axis uses whole-thousands (`$Xk`) formatting. A $400 expense renders as a full-height bar against five ticks all labelled \"$0k\", making a non-zero value indistinguishable from zero.\n\nTwo notes on scope: state is held in memory (no `localStorage`), so I avoided page reloads throughout. The Reports month selector only offers the trailing 12 months, so the seeded 2024 data wasn't reachable there — CT-21 was verified against current-month figures I controlled directly. A pre-existing React \"unique key prop\" console error in `TaxSummary` is present but non-fatal and didn't affect print."
  }
}
